Fixed the performance mode button.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 06:55:00

Profile hotkeys and single instance. New module instance.py: the app listens on a per-user QLocalServer
(bc250-governor-manager-<uid>); a second launch forwards "show" (raise the window) or "profile NAME" and exits,
so no second poller or tray icon appears, and a stale socket from a crash is cleared. New command-line flags:
--profile NAME applies a saved profile in the running instance or starts the app and applies it (unknown names
give a tray warning and status-bar text, no dialog); --list-profiles prints the names. The Profiles box has
"Copy hotkey command", which puts `<launcher> --profile 'Name'` (shell-quoted, tray.profile_command) on the
clipboard for System Settings → Shortcuts; true global shortcuts were not used because the Wayland
GlobalShortcuts portal is not reliable across KDE, GNOME and Gamescope. 5 new tests (socket forward/listen/stale
recovery, request handling, clipboard command). Help, README and the hardware checklist updated. New test.sh
runs the suite with the project venv (installs pytest there on first use, extra arguments go to pytest).

Changelog: 07-10-2026 06:45:00

Overview: compare the live session with an earlier CSV export. New "Compare…" button loads a file written by
"Export CSV…" (history.read_csv, tolerant to blank cells and missing optional columns, refuses foreign files)
and draws its load, temperature and clock as dashed, thinner lines in the same colors behind the live ones,
right-aligned like the live window and following the Window combo; the note under the chart shows the
reference's duration, average load/clock/temperature/power and peaks next to the same figures for the live
window (history.Summary/summarize). "Clear" removes the reference. Help, README and the hardware checklist
updated; 3 new tests (CSV round-trip and summary, bad-file handling, overlay/notes/clear).

Changelog: 07-10-2026 06:35:00

Safe points: while a point is pinned the kernel log is watched. New module kernelwatch.py tails journalctl -k -f
in a QProcess and matches amdgpu/SMU trouble (ring timeouts, GPU reset, [drm] *ERROR*, soft recovery, failed
to set/send/load, SMU failed/timed out/"not done with your previous command", MODE1/2 reset); the first match
aborts the test immediately (performance mode off, load tool killed), the verdict quotes the line and the count
of further ones and the tray message uses the warning icon. A clean run reports "no GPU errors in the kernel
log"; when the kernel ring is not readable (user not in systemd-journal/wheel) the live status and verdict say
the log is not watched. The four test-ending paths share a new MainWindow._end_test helper. 17 new tests
(pattern matching, watch bookkeeping, abort flow, late lines ignored, clean verdict). Help, README and the
hardware checklist (/dev/kmsg injection) updated.

