Changelog: 07-10-2026 06:15:00

Release 0.3.0. The release workflow now runs the pytest suite before tagging, releases a __version__ that is
newer than every tag as written (so a deliberate minor bump ships as x.y.0 instead of x.y.1) and otherwise
increments the latest tag's patch number as before. .gitattributes keeps tests/, .github/, requirements-dev.txt
and the dot-files out of the release tarball.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 06:05:00

Test suite: tests/ with 41 pytest cases (conftest.py: offscreen QApplication, temporary config.toml, snapshot
factory): config.toml schema round-trip for every GovernorConfig field, section appending after
[[safe-points]], unchanged-value preservation, compact floats, optional keys, tt subset, validate() rejections;
safe-point parsing/rendering and the interpolation helper; AlertMonitor edge/hysteresis/cooldown/service
rules; History ring buffer, CSV export and the Overview chart window; ProfileStore round-trip and tolerance to
old files; StressRunner with fake tools; MainWindow TestMode state machine (start, stop, timer, Performance
action, governor gone, close), profile save/load/apply/delete and Performance-page prefill/validation with the
bus, systemd and dialogs mocked. requirements-dev.txt (pytest), .github/workflows/tests.yml runs the suite on
every push and pull request, .pytest_cache ignored, README Development section documents it.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 05:50:00

Safe points: the point test can now load the GPU itself. A "Load" combo lists the load generators found on PATH
(vkmark, glmark2-wayland, glmark2, vkcube, glxgears); the chosen one is started with the test and killed when
the test ends by any path (Stop, timer, close, Performance-page action, governor gone). If the tool exits or
crashes while the point is pinned, the live status and the result flag it. The result line now reports the
held time, peak temperature and clock range from the telemetry history. New "Add to table" button inserts the
tested pair into the safe-points table (sorted, replacing a point at the same frequency). New module stress.py
(available_tools, StressRunner on QProcess). test_requested signal gained the tool name. Help and README updated.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 05:40:00

Overview: the chart keeps an hour of telemetry (one sample per 2 s poll) instead of two minutes; a "Window"
combo shows the last 2, 10, 30 or 60 minutes, right-aligned so the newest sample is always at the right edge,
and the box title says how much is recorded. "Export CSV…" writes every kept sample (time, load %, clock MHz,
temperature, socket power W, performance mode, runtime range) to a file. New module history.py (Sample,
History, default_csv_name); series are now redrawn with QLineSeries.replace(). Help and README updated.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 05:30:00

Alerts: new "Alerts" box on the Settings page with three switches: GPU temperature reaching a chosen value
(default 80 °C), GPU reaching the governor's throttling temperature (runtime value over D-Bus, else config.toml),
and the governor service stopping or failing after the app has seen it running. Shown as tray notifications,
and in the status bar; edge-triggered with 5 °C hysteresis and a 5-minute cooldown per alert kind so a hot
session gives one message, not one per poll. New module alerts.py (AlertMonitor, AlertSettings). Help and README
updated.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 05:20:00

Named profiles: a "Profiles" box at the top of the Tuning page saves the current Tuning + GPU Usage values under
a name (per user, ~/.config/bc250-governor-manager/profiles.json), loads a profile into the forms for review,
applies one directly to config.toml (backup, pkexec, governor restart; pending edits are discarded after a
confirmation) or deletes it. Safe points are not part of a profile. The tray menu gets an "Apply profile"
submenu. New module profiles.py; ConfigPage.show_values() fills a form without changing its saved baseline.
Help and README updated.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 05:10:00

Performance page: runtime "Set load target" (lower/upper %) and "Set temperatures" (throttling / recovery, 0 =
not set) controls on the existing SetLoadTarget and SetTemperatureThresholds D-Bus methods. The forms follow the
governor's current values and are only refilled when those change, so polling does not overwrite edits;
invalid pairs disable the button with a hint. These calls do not end a running safe-point test (the governor
only clears test mode on Enabled, SetFixedFrequency and SetRange). Help and README updated.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 04:55:00

Safe points page: "Test a point before saving it" uses the governor's root-only TestMode D-Bus interface
(SetTestMode over pkexec busctl) to pin a frequency and voltage at runtime without touching config.toml; the
governor stops scaling, thermal throttling stays on. Fields prefilled from the selected row (top point on load),
warnings above 2000 MHz / 1000 mV and when the voltage is below the curve's interpolation, confirmation dialog, timer
(default 60 s, 0 = until stopped) with countdown in the status line, Stop test. The test ends via Enabled=false
(start-up range restored) on Stop, timer, app close, any Performance-page call, or when the governor goes away. The
box is hidden for backends without D-Bus (tt). dbus.py: set_test_mode(); the TestMode exclusion note is gone.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 04:40:00

The remaining config.toml sections of the governor are now managed. GPU Usage page: [gpu] set-method (smu or
kernel). Tuning page, now in two columns: [timing.intervals] sample/adjust (µs), [timing.ramp-rates] normal/burst
(MHz/ms), [timing] burst-samples (Off = key left out, 1..64) and down-events, and [frequency-thresholds] adjust (the
dead band). Validation follows the governor: adjust >= sample, burst rate above normal. Presets leave the timing
alone. The tt backend gets the timing and threshold sections too (without down-events, which it lacks); [gpu] is
smu-only. Backend: unchanged values are compared numerically (1 vs 1.00, 100_000 vs 100000), so lines that already
mean the same stay byte-identical; floats are written compactly (0.65, 1.0). Fix: a [[safe-points]] header now ends
the preceding section, so a key appended to e.g. [temperature] no longer lands inside the last safe point.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 04:25:00

Version 0.2.0 (the release workflow still adds the patch number on top). Power is now shown in watts: the
Cyan Skillfish SMU puts 24.8 fixed-point values into the gpu_metrics power fields (raw 4000-8000 = 15-31 W),
the same >>8 amdgpu's hwmon code applies; the Overview detail shows the raw value next to it. A GPU load
reading that vanishes for a poll (the governor replaces its patched table on every flush) is held for up to
6 s instead of flashing N/A.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 04:30:00

Second backend: cyan-skillfish-governor-tt (the tt branch) via --backend tt, or --backend auto (default) which
picks the governor whose systemd unit is loaded. CyanSkillfishTtBackend subclasses the smu backend with its own
unit, package, config path, schema ([load-target], [temperature] only), default safe points and no features
(gpu-usage, frequency-range, dbus); read/render now use the per-class schema. The main window hides the GPU
Usage and Performance pages, the frequency-range and dbus Tuning sections, the gpu_metrics/performance pills and
the update check for backends without them; presets then only set load and temperature. Diagnostics report the
backend's package. --config defaults to the backend's path.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 04:15:00

Safe points page is now an editor: spin boxes per row, Add point (halfway to the next), Remove, Sort, Shipped
defaults (the governor's default-config.toml table), Revert, Apply with restart option. Validation blocks Apply on
the governor's rules (>= 2 points, unique frequencies, voltage never drops with rising frequency) and the hard
rails shared with bc250-gpu-oc-bisect (700-1100 mV, <= 2500 MHz); warnings above 2000 MHz / 1000 mV and when a
change raises the top frequency or lowers an existing voltage. Backend: render_safe_points() replaces the active
[[safe-points]] blocks in place (commented ones stay), write_safe_points() installs with backup via pkexec.
Dirty safe points count for the close confirmation; status bar lists dirty pages by name.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 04:00:00

Governor update check: Service page "Check for updates" compares rpm -q cyan-skillfish-governor-smu with the latest
GitHub release of filippor/cyan-skillfish-governor (QThread, 10 s timeout, never blocks). Version row in the unit
box with a link to the release; newer release in orange, status-bar and tray notice. Settings: "Check for a newer
governor release when the app starts" (default on).

Changelog: 07-10-2026 03:50:00

Performance page: the static Steam examples became a "Per game" generator for the cyan-skillfish-performance-mode
wrapper. Modes: performance mode, --fixed-frequency, --range, --load-target, --temperature, with inputs prefilled
from the governor's runtime state, validation (min < max, recovery < throttle), output formatted for Steam launch
options, Heroic/Lutris wrapper command or a terminal, and a Copy button. Verified against the wrapper script in
the governor repo (one option per call; Enabled=false on exit restores the start-up range).

Changelog: 07-10-2026 03:40:00

Service page: "Export diagnostics…" saves a text file for bug reports with app/governor/Bazzite versions, CPU and
GPU, config.toml and its backups, systemctl status/cat, the last 300 journal lines, the D-Bus interface, kernel
command line, amdgpu kernel messages, hwmon sensors and the raw gpu_metrics table (parsed + hex dump). The bug
report issue template now asks for that file instead of separate pastes.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 04:05:00

New Settings page (app settings, stored per user with QSettings). System tray icon: tooltip with GPU load, clock,
temperature, performance mode and governor state; left-click shows/hides the window; menu toggles performance
mode over D-Bus and quits. Optional close-to-tray. Login autostart writes ~/.config/autostart/bc250-governor-
manager.desktop (uses the install.sh launcher when present), optionally with the new --start-in-tray flag.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 03:30:00

The Service page journal is now a live tail (journalctl -u … -f via QProcess) instead of a 100-line snapshot
polled every two seconds: filter box (text or regex, case-insensitive), Follow toggle, Clear, up to 2000 lines
kept, restarts itself if journalctl ends, and only runs while the page is shown.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 03:20:00

New Safe points page: the [[safe-points]] of config.toml as a table and a frequency/voltage curve (read-only),
with the governor's allowed range when D-Bus is reachable. New Backups page: lists config.toml.bak-* copies,
shows a unified diff against the current file and restores one with pkexec (current file backed up first,
optional governor restart). The Overview chart now plots temperature and clock next to the load (left axis
% / °C, right axis MHz); missing readings leave a gap.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 02:45:00

Fixed: the gpu_metrics header was read in the wrong field order (structure_size comes first), so every table
was rejected and the GPU load, power and gpu_metrics box stayed empty. Header box renamed to Performance mode.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 01:40:00

install.sh and a desktop entry: the release tarball now installs as a normal desktop app for the current user
(private venv under ~/.local/share, launcher in ~/.local/bin, menu entry with icon), with --uninstall. The
