Changelog: 07-10-2026 02:10:00

New Tuning page: [frequency-range] min/max (0 = no limit), [load-target] upper/lower, [temperature] throttling
and optional throttling_recovery, [dbus] enabled, with presets (Shipped defaults, Quiet, Responsive, Maximum
clock) and validation. Apply on either config page writes the pending edits of both; the config writer is now
schema-driven, keeps comments and spacing, revives commented-out optional keys in place and creates missing
sections.

New Performance page: performance mode on/off, pinned frequency and runtime range over the governor's D-Bus
interface (busctl, no password), with the current/initial/allowed ranges and targets, a copy-to-Tuning button
and the Steam launch options of cyan-skillfish-performance-mode. Controls are disabled with a reason when the
service is down or [dbus] is off.

The gpu_metrics v2.1/v2.2 table is parsed as a struct; the Overview shows activities, temperatures, power,
clocks, throttle status and CPU core clocks, marked (patched) or (raw). The header gained Power (socket) and
Perf. mode boxes; clock and temperature fall back to gpu_metrics when hwmon has no sensor.

Changelog: 07-10-2026 00:35:00

GPU load is now read from the governor's patched gpu_metrics table (average_gfx_activity, the field the governor
writes) while it is mounted; gpu_busy_percent and radeontop are fallbacks. Previously the load was Unavailable
on a BC-250 even with the governor running. When no source is usable, the load box and the Overview pill say
what to do (install the governor, enable fix-metrics, start the service, check the journal).

Changelog: 06-10-2026 23:55:00

First working version, laid out like bc250-bazzite-test: logo and metric boxes (GPU load, clock, temperature,
load method, governor state) on top, navigation on the left (Overview, GPU Usage, Service, Help), Fusion style
with the system palette, purple accent, rounded tooltips, Inter header font on Linux. Window size and last
page are remembered.

Backend fixed: the methods of CyanSkillfishBackend had fallen out of the class (wrong indentation after
installation_status), so nothing worked. Package renamed to bc250_governor.backends, entry point is
python -m bc250_governor (the old bc250_governor/main.py could not be run from the repository root).

[gpu-usage] editor now covers the whole section of the SMU governor: fix-metrics, fix-freq, method,
temp-read and flush-every. Existing lines keep indentation and trailing comments, missing keys are appended
to the section, the legacy [gpu_usage] spelling is read too. Backup and write go through a single pkexec
call; an unchanged file is not written. Apply is only enabled when a value differs from the file.

Service page: start, stop, restart, enable and disable, systemctl status, last 100 journal lines. Status
comes from one systemctl show call (LoadState/ActiveState/SubState/UnitFileState). gpu_metrics override
detection checks whether the file itself is a mount point (findmnt without -T) on every AMD card. GPU clock
and temperature from the amdgpu hwmon sensors. A system without systemd/findmnt (development) no longer
raises; --config PATH points the app at a test file.

Repository: python/ venv like the reference project, icons/ removed, tree.txt regenerated, README rewritten.
